{"abstract":[{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Documentation index","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/RoundTrip\/documentation\/RoundTrip","isActive":true,"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"Documentation index"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/RoundTrip\/documentation\/RoundTrip\/Downloads","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Downloads","modules":[{"name":"RoundTrip"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/RoundTrip\/documentation\/RoundTrip"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/roundtrip\/downloads"]}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RoundTrip\/documentation\/RoundTrip\/Adapters","doc:\/\/RoundTrip\/documentation\/RoundTrip\/Multipart","doc:\/\/RoundTrip\/documentation\/RoundTrip\/WebSockets"],"anchor":"Transfers","title":"Transfers","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"download(request:to:progress:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to move a completed download to a destination URL. The destination must be writable and should not already contain a file.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let destination = try FileManager.default","    .url(for: .documentDirectory, in: .userDomainMask, appropriateFor: nil, create: true)","    .appending(path: \"report.pdf\")","","let request = URLRequestBuilder(string: \"https:\/\/example.com\/report.pdf\")!","let response = try await HttpClient().download(request: request, to: destination)","try response.checkForStatusCodeValidity(validStatusCode: [200])"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/RoundTrip\/documentation\/RoundTrip\/BackgroundHttpClient"},{"text":" when an Apple app needs system-managed background transfers. Set its ","type":"text"},{"code":"completionHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the application’s background-session event callback, and observe ","type":"text"},{"code":"finishedTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the main actor.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Releasing a background client lets its existing transfers and delegate callbacks finish. The session then invalidates and releases its resources. Keep the client alive while observing ","type":"text"},{"code":"finishedTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; its ","type":"text"},{"code":"completionHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remains available to the session until background events finish, even after the client is released. The handler is cleared and called once on the main actor; install a new handler for each background-session event callback. Completed downloads are still moved into the download cache.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancel a transfer explicitly by calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSessionDownloadTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSessionUploadTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returned by the client. Releasing the client does not cancel those tasks. Retain and reuse a client for a given background-session identifier while its transfers are active; do not create a replacement session with that identifier while the previous session is finishing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://RoundTrip/documentation/RoundTrip":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Build requests and perform HTTP transfers on Apple platforms.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/RoundTrip\/documentation\/RoundTrip","title":"RoundTrip","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/roundtrip"},"doc://RoundTrip/documentation/RoundTrip